00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.210
that's whenever it starts,
because at six hours,

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:25.010
that it's already processed
through your body.

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:27.670
At 12 hours, that's
whenever the withdrawal

00:05:27.670 --> 00:05:31.160
actually is in full motion.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:36.160
And with fentanyl, it attacks
your central nervous system

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:41.240
and it, certain
neurotransmitters in your head,

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:44.970
and it's tied to your dopamine.

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:47.260
And what it does is like

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.610
this is like your dopamine regularly.

00:05:49.610 --> 00:05:51.460
This is it with fentanyl.

00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:54.570
It just puts a mask on it, you know?

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:59.570
And it completely replaces
them, certain ones anyway.

00:06:01.090 --> 00:06:02.660
So whenever you don't have that, it's like

00:06:02.660 --> 00:06:06.640
my body's missing
certain things, you know,

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:11.600
